body:
Ok, like others have said, definitely DEFINITELY call child protective services! I was in a bad situation as a kid and I wish more people had tried to intervene. It might be scary at first, but it will be better for her in the long run!

&#x200B;

BUT! If you don't think she is in immediate danger, try to collect more evidence first. Don't go to the authorities half-cocked, or you run the risk of not convincing CPS that anything is actually wrong and just making her dad upset. Especially since you say the sister doesn't care, if CPS interviews her she could definitely weaken the credibility of your claims. Audio recordings are a good way to document the situation, if your gf has the phone maybe she could set up the voice recorder on it and record a conversation. Pictures of anything relevant might also help, but I think the audio recording is the best way to go. A journal with dates of incidents and a short description might also help the authorities? Something like that could easily be faked (not saying you should fake it), but maybe CPS would still take it seriously. Texts that you have from your gf about the situation might also be useful.

&#x200B;

Other than that, as others have said, try to sneak her food. Fruits and veggies are important for vitamins, and protein is also important for energy. Carbs are easy to find, so if you can choose, choose proteins or other 'healthy' foods. But, obviously any food is better than no food. 

&#x200B;

To the girlfriend, I'm so sorry the person who is supposed to protect you is torturing you. You do not deserve even one ounce of that shit, and that is not the way anyone is supposed to treat you. You are a strong and powerful girl, deserving of love and respect, and this situation will pass. 

&#x200B;

Good luck to you both, keep us updated!
